# Feature 004 (spec A-10): after an operation that changes an app's state the list shows its first page again; after a look at a detail page with
# no change it keeps its page. The demo catalog has 14 apps on three pages (the banner takes a row from each) (the app with the update is on the first).
# scenario demo
size 1404 1872
wait 400
tap refresh
waitfor catalogLine Catalog last updated
waitfor appRow
# part 1: Update all started from page 2 ends on page 1
tap pageDown
expect pageIndicator 2 / 3
tap updateAllButton
waitfor updateAllIntro
tap consent 0
tap consent 1
tap confirm
waitfor resultText Updated:
tap ok
waitfor appRow
# (nothing is left to update, so the banner is gone and the list is back to two pages)
expect pageIndicator 1 / 2
expect_disabled pageUp
# part 2: a look at a detail page with no change keeps the page
tap pageDown
expect pageIndicator 2 / 2
tap appRow 0
waitfor detailState
tap back
expect pageIndicator 2 / 2
# (a single update needs no walk of its own here: an app with an update is always on page 1 because updatable apps are listed first)
quit
